
    tclpdf - PDF generation for Tcl


    This directory contains a freely distributable pure tcl extension called tclpdf.


SYNOPSIS

    Create PDF documents from Tcl: pages, graphics, embedded fonts, images,
    tables and electronic invoices.

    The package covers what jsPDF and jsPDF-AutoTable provide, plus two things
    they do not: general file attachments and reusable form XObjects.

        Document and graphics
            Pages, paths, transparency (ExtGState), form XObjects for reusable
            content, RGB / CMYK / separation colours, clipping and shadings.

        Fonts
            Embed TrueType fonts as Type0/CIDFontType2 with Identity-H and a
            ToUnicode CMap, subset down to the glyphs actually used. A missing
            character raises an error instead of silently disappearing.

        Images
            JPEG and PNG. Both are passed through unchanged wherever possible:
            a JPEG stream goes in as /DCTDecode, a PNG without alpha as
            /FlateDecode with /Predictor 15 - neither is ever decoded.

        Tables
            Column widths, cell wrapping, page breaks with repeated header and
            footer rows, rowSpan/colSpan and per-cell hooks.

        Electronic invoices
            ZUGFeRD / Factur-X as PDF/A-3B: ICC profile, OutputIntent, XMP with
            the Factur-X extension schema, embedded XML, file specification,
            /AF entry and name tree. The conformance level is derived from
            BT-24 of the invoice XML rather than taken on trust.

    See docs/FEATURES.md for the full scope, what was deliberately left out,
    and the measurements behind each decision.


DEPENDENCIES

    Tcl >= 8.6.11 (runs under Tcl 9 as well)

    The core needs nothing beyond Tcl itself: zlib is a built-in command,
    not a package. Optional, each for one feature only:

        tdom     - only for the SVG module
        TclTLS   - only for encryption (tls::encrypt is roughly 1000 times
                   faster than a pure-Tcl AES; without it, encryption is
                   unavailable rather than slow)
        tzint    - only for barcodes and QR codes

    Tk is not required and must not be pulled in.


GETTING THE CODE

    The development repository is hosted at https://fossil.sowaswie.de/tclpdf
    You are encouraged to use trunk.


INSTALLING

    Simply extract the download tclpdf-<version>.zip into your Tcl library path.

    Since tclpdf is TEA-compatible you should be able to do

        ./configure
        make test
        make install

    By default this installs into the lib directory of the Tcl
    installation found by configure (use --with-tcl to point it to the
    tclConfig.sh of another Tcl), so that this tclsh finds the package
    on its auto_path. To install into a different location use

        ./configure --prefix /path/to/tree

    which installs the package into /path/to/tree/lib/tclpdf<version>.


REPORTING BUGS

    Please head to https://fossil.sowaswie.de/tclpdf/ticket and
    click on "New Ticket". Log in as anonymous and report your findings.
    If you prefer to have an individual login write Alex a mail.


HISTORY

